{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1793953025937-reviewer-h3-6-audit.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-06 08:29:28 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-06 15:29:28 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nAudit did not pass. Two actionable findings remain:\n\n- **P1 | test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2411 |** The “canonical” hash includes unstable reader-generated symbols. Reading identical pinned NBE source twice produces different `p1__…#` names and hashes. Fresh recomputation mismatches **60/155 fixtures**; the hash guard correctly refuses them, leaving **46/165 arities credited**. Consequently, the companion file fails byte-for-byte reproduction. **Concrete fix:** deterministically canonicalize generated binders before hashing, regenerate evidence, and add a fresh-process hash reproducibility regression.\n\n- **P2 | test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3097 |** Case 6 silently skips its dynamic-site assertion: the selected fixture contains **zero dynamic sites**. Capturing assertion reports during execution confirmed that this assertion never fires. **Concrete fix:** use a fixture containing an executed indirect call, assert that its dynamic site exists, and execute the refusal assertion unconditionally.\n\nVerified independently:\n\n- Raw traces reconstruct **165/165** using recorded hashes, without trusting coverage entries; all **563 witness paths** match.\n- All **20,805 site rows** reproduce exactly. The companion file differs only in the 60 hashes.\n- Stale diagnostics match exactly: **14,307 sites across 113 fixtures**, maximum **401 per fixture**, all referencing existing sites.\n- **56,994 dynamic-site probes** produced no cross-arity borrowing.\n- Removing instrumentation restores every original compiled AST exactly.\n- Five focused tests passed: **152 assertions, zero failures or errors**.\n\nNo repository files were edited.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
