ntlr-test` 3183 s (about 1580 s alone on the laptop) |\n425:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"\n465:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"\n484:Two Linux x86_64 servers run the full suite faster than a laptop. Both are\n517:branch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\n518:the host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\n538:scratch clone, whose local `master` ref had not moved since October 26 because\n557:reports without comparing it to the hash your push from the laptop printed.\n566:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\n581:CPU: they exist because a laptop has 8 cores. They are not a rule about repos.\n583:avoidable\"). The laptop additionally never runs the slow tier or the nightly\n602:- Do not treat this as permission to overlap lanes on the laptop.\n729:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"\n766:### Known differences from the laptop\n830:it, against about 9 minutes on the 8-core laptop run alone. Prerequisites (`npm ci`,\n835:\"free laptop\" comparison predates the 2026-11-04 ruling that suite-scale runs\n845:laptop — route Node lanes to shiva; the laptop comparison is historical and\n868:orchestrator's laptop. This generalizes this section from \"run tests remotely\n872:orchestrator's laptop unloaded.\n877:1. **Land the branch on origin first** (push from the laptop; never rsync) and\n894:   from the orchestrator's laptop while a remote agent owns the same gate.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
